    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, the customer needs to make a purchase and then connect to the website."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly triggers the process start (init) and describes the initial combined action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, they should search for an item."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the sequential search step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4",
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If they choose to \"Add item to cart\", they can proceed to checkout."
      ],
      "justification": "The choice introduces the action node and XOR branch; the guard and subsequent action faithfully restate the positive arm condition and outcome."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if they select \"Continue Shopping\", they should continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard and action accurately capture the negative arm condition and corresponding flow."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once they proceed to checkout, they need to enter their address, shipping method, and payment information."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact match for the checkout data entry step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "At the same time, they should also authorize the credit card and check the inventory levels."
      ],
      "justification": "Concurrency keywords justify the AND branch and converge nodes, while the action restates the simultaneous tasks."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the credit card is approved and there is inventory in stock, they can continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Action node captures the compound success condition; implicit XOR branch opens the evaluation path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In either case, the order confirmation number should be displayed, followed by the final order being shown to the customer."
      ],
      "justification": "Both actions directly correspond to the sequential post-condition outputs."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13",
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, the order should be confirmed and a confirmation notice should be emailed to the customer."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct mapping of the two concluding administrative steps."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the order entry is complete, the process will end."
      ],
      "justification": "Action states the completion milestone; structural end node aligns with the explicit termination statement."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the credit card is denied or there is no inventory in stock, the transaction will end."
      ],
      "justification": "Action and structural end node correctly model the failure path termination."
    }
  ],
